in the international constitution tournament!

263
00:14:19,950 --> 00:14:21,260
This is a problem, Ryo-san.

264
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,350
It can't be helped.

265
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,100
I'll compete in his place as a trainee.

266
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:27,440
Tara-san!

267
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,680
That's not the problem!

268
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:33,140
The problem is this beard!

269
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:36,980
A beard? A beard grows back in a month!

270
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,360
I didn't grow it for nothing, that beard!

271
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:42,200
That beard is a beard of happiness!

272
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,920
A beard of happiness?
What's that supposed to mean?

273
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:48,680
I hope nothing unfortunate happens.

274
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:50,840
Will something bad happen
if I shave my beard?

275
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:55,180
Recently, just days after
accidentally shaving off only one side,

276
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:57,560
it happened.

277
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:00,460
Before that, there was also the
collapse of the bubble economy,

278
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:01,460
the Heisei rice riots, and so on.

279
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,820
All kinds of misfortune happened
Translation>
right when I shaved this beard off.

280
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:04,720
Every single time.

281
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:08,260
Isn't that a misfortune
beard instead of a lucky beard?

282
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:09,260
No.

283
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:11,860
The reason my husband became
a successful martial artist

284
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,720
and the reason we were able to get married

285
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:16,320
is that he started growing the lucky beard.

286
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,940
At the international
constitution tournament,

287
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,340
I just hope nothing happens.

288
00:15:26,780 --> 00:15:30,900
We will now open the 107th
International Constitutional Convention.

289
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:36,880
And now, we will hear opening remarks from Elder Chang Nian-tian,
a resident of the China section.

290
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,520
I'm Chang Nian-tian, you know.

291
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,900
Darling hasn't arrived yet?

292
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:46,700
That's right. What should I do?
It's going to start!

293
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:51,340
That's strange. I left first,
saying I'd take his lunch with me.

294
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:55,120
Could his misfortune have already started?

295
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,420
It's no good,
there's no sign of movement at all.

296
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:05,020
It was clear until just now, but at this rate
we won't make it to the convention in time.

297
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:07,300
There's no choice.
I'll get off the expressway alone.

298
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:07,800
Yes.

299
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:12,480
Ever since morning, I've tripped and things have fallen on me.
It's nothing but bad luck.

300
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:16,400
It must be because I dropped my lucky day.

301
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:17,880
Hey, taxi!

302
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:19,640
Hey, stop!

303
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,320
Damn it, he's completely ignoring me.

304
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:25,180
Wow, so you're saying this
is because of the beard too?

305
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:43,940
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

306
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:46,240
Damn it,
disqualified before I even got started!

307
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:50,120
Now, first round, begin!

308
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,360
It's already started!

309
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,600
Please, Ryo-san, can't you do something?

310
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:58,540
Even if you say that,
there's only so much I can do!

311
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:00,140
Ryo-san, you can do it!

312
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,540
Please, do something!

313
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,620
What a predicament.

314
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,220
Ippon!

315
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:08,940
Ai-Rai-Ken wins!

316
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:12,340
Senpai, it's your turn next!

317
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:14,240
Ryo-san.

318
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,140
Alright, I'll handle this.

319
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,464
Now, representing Honda,
Rock-ken, versus Asato-ban,

320
00:17:20,514 --> 00:17:22,760
Rock-paper-scissors representatives: rock,
scissors, paper!

321
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,420
I'm the referee.

322
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:30,180
No, I'm not like that at all.

323
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:32,500
More importantly, can we win?

324
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,180
Then, begin!

325
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:37,900
Honda Raken's bewitching technique,
the Dance of Spit!

326
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:39,900
He's crying!

327
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,440
Now!

328
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:46,580
Point! The winner is Honda Raken!

329
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:49,220
We did it!
That move looks just like someone!

330
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:50,340
Indeed.

331
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,720
Yeah, copying Honda-ra's father isn't easy,
you know.

332
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:56,209
Next, representing Honda Raken,

333
00:17:56,259 --> 00:17:59,520
Ryotsu Kanki Zone.
Representing Yakyūken, Yoyoi-no-I.

334
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,680
Now it's my turn.

335
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:06,660
Cars are out. Let's take the subway.

336
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,120
This way, we'll arrive on time.

337
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:28,660
What a flashy move!

338
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:31,840
Ippon! That's the match!

339
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:36,940
What the hell are you doing,
you old fool Honda!

340
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:39,600
After all, your own two legs are the best!

341
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:44,920
Oh my God!
Why is the lid of the magic style open?

342
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,700
Stay away!

343
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,300
It's a white crocodile!

344
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,940
I can't take it, I can't take it...

345
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,300
It's a bear cub!

346
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:21,780
Don't come over here!

347
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:23,100
It's him!

348
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:25,380
Help!

349
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:30,340
Trier!

350
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,060
Exactly!

351
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:36,680
That's thirteen down without a break!

352
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,583
The next semifinal is

353
00:19:38,633 --> 00:19:41,020
representing Hondara Prefecture,
Asato Manta!

354
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,160
So busy!

355
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,620
representing Franken, Jumbo Yamashita!

356
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:52,840
W-is this guy really human?

357
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,020
Aaaaaaah!

358
00:19:55,020 --> 00:19:55,560
Aaaaaaah!

359
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,760
Aaaaaaah!

360
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:09,720
When did we even get to the Arctic Ocean?

361
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,820
Aaaaaaah!

362
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:13,600
Amazing!

363
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,740
We did it, we're going to the finals!

364
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:19,020
Nihon Asadoban wins!

365
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:21,180
Bring it on, whatever it is!

366
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,320
Remote Control Prefecture,
the entire territory!

367
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,080
Yeah, yeah.

368
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:27,980
Representing Remote Control Prefecture,
Mecha Mecha Robot-kun!

369
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,380
That's allowed?!

370
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:35,140
Hurry, my comrades!
We must return to Japan quickly!

371
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:40,260
A vessel of unknown nationality, possibly.
No response.

372
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:42,020
Never mind. Attack.

373
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:42,740
Roger!

374
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,860
Why won't it come out!

375
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:54,320
Somehow, it's this one

376
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:56,180
Where are you taking me?

377
00:20:58,180 --> 00:20:59,080
This one too

378
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:02,600
Just snatch the remote and it's ours.

379
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:04,480
We won!

380
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:05,560
That's amazing!

381
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:08,500
With this, both of Honda's
men have advanced to the final!

382
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:09,860
Both of them?

383
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:12,800
Senpai, what are we going to do?

384
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,420
Next up is the final match.

385
00:21:16,420 --> 00:21:20,920
The winner will receive
a prize of 10 million yen.

386
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:26,900
I didn't hear about that!
Then put Old Honda in danger!

387
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:28,500
That's the problem.

388
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:32,680
If the final doesn't go ahead,
the prize money won't be paid out.

389
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:36,080
Hey! Damn it, there has to be some way.

390
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:42,220
N-no! At this rate,
the tournament is going to end!

391
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:44,760
Whoa! They've caught up and appeared!

392
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:47,620
Help!

393
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:52,820
Let's somehow use these
dolls to cover it up.

394
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:54,120
Really?

395
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,300
This is going to be very difficult.

396
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,220
Now then, Honda Ken, Azato Bantain.

397
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:02,960
Likewise, the final match by Honda Ken,
Ryotsu Kankichi.

398
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:08,160
It seems it has already started.

399
00:22:14,340 --> 00:22:14,940
I can't see!

400
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:25,620
Ippon!

401
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:30,740
Yes! I've finally made
it past the fourth round!

402
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:41,000
What's going on here?

403
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,620
Morning and night, there are two of them?

404
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,360
Aw, geez!

405
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,040
W-where is this?

406
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:55,660
Damn it!
I was going to win and get ten million yen!

407
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:57,580
Showing up at the worst possible moment!

408
00:22:58,340 --> 00:22:59,560
So that's how it is.

409
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:03,600
Come on, Ryotsu! The real match starts now!

410
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:04,120
Yeah.

411
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,300
Bring it on.

412
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:12,780
It's for ten million yen. I can't lose!

413
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:15,800
I'll show you!

414
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:21,860
Here I come, bring it!

415
00:23:51,260 --> 00:23:52,420
The one who got flipped over is you!

416
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:56,640
Damn it! Hurry up and grow that beard!

417
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,480
At this rate, we'll turn into Mars!

418
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,700
Shocked and making a commotion

419
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:18,320
Yaaah!

420
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,240
with a battle cry

421
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:19,700
No, no!

422
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:20,660
and settled it

423
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:21,380
Please, please!

424
00:24:21,380 --> 00:24:22,260
and swiftly

425
00:24:22,260 --> 00:24:22,820
Whoa!

426
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:23,560
and wipe it out

427
00:24:24,220 --> 00:24:25,080
Rock bottom

428
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:27,000
Dede!

429
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:27,920
it's been decided,

430
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,380
and an idea struck!

431
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:30,020
Oryaaa!

432
00:24:30,020 --> 00:24:30,880
bouncing along,

433
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:31,480
Deberade!

434
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:32,360
and wrapping it all up,

435
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:32,940
Flustered!

436
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:33,840
and into action!

437
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:35,620
flying over here,

438
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:39,880
above all, power for sumo!

439
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,560
everyone, gather!

440
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:45,880
if you come here,

441
00:24:49,540 --> 00:24:52,220
The last energy

442
00:24:53,460 --> 00:24:56,720
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

443
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,620
painting the universe,
standing on the ground,

444
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,340
the star of Kameari comes rolling in,
how strange that is!

445
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,060
This should be fine, right?

446
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:08,540
Like hell it is!

447
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:25,240
What, you came down
from heaven to punish me?

448
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:27,380
Don't make me laugh, you goddamn old geezer.

449
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:31,980
Whoa, what the hell?
Why have I shrunk this much?

450
00:25:32,580 --> 00:25:34,840
Next time: Ryo-san shrinks!

451
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:37,500
I was wrong, please change me back!

